<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="EPH" style="id">EPHESIANS</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="EPH 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Apostolic Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 1:1"/>
    Paul, called to be an apostle of Christ Jesus through the sovereign will of God,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To God’s consecrated people living in Ephesus, those who remain steadfast in their union with Christ Jesus:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 1:2"/>
    May grace or undeserved favour and peace be yours from God our Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Ascription of Praise to God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 1:3"/>
    Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has lavished upon us every spiritual gift from the heavenly realm through our union with Christ.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 1:4"/>
    He chose us to belong to Christ before the world was created, with the intention that we would live in holiness and without fault in His presence, motivated by love.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 1:5"/>
    He determined beforehand that we would be brought into His family as His sons and daughters through Jesus Christ, fulfilling His own gracious intention and desire,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 1:6"/>
    all for the purpose of bringing praise to His magnificent grace, which He has generously bestowed on us through His beloved Son.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 1:7"/>
    Through Him we have been liberated through His sacrificial blood, receiving forgiveness for our violations of God’s Law, in keeping with the abundant wealth of His grace,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 1:8"/>
    which He poured out upon us with complete wisdom and spiritual insight.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 1:9"/>
    God revealed to us the hidden purpose of His will, in accordance with His gracious plan that He determined in Christ
    <verse eid="EPH 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 1:10"/>
    to be carried out when the fullness of the appointed times unfolds—namely, to bring everything together under Christ’s headship—all things in heaven and all things on earth—yes, in Him alone.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 1:11"/>
    In Christ we have also received our appointed inheritance, having been chosen beforehand according to the predetermined plan of the One who accomplishes all things in harmony with the decision of His will,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 1:12"/>
    so that we who were the first to place our hope in Christ would live for the praise of His magnificent character.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 1:13"/>
    In Him you also were included when you heard the message of truth—the good news of your salvation—and having placed your trust in Him, you were marked with the seal of the promised Holy Spirit,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 1:14"/>
    who serves as the down payment guaranteeing our inheritance until God fully redeems those who are His own possession, resulting in praise to His glory.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer for the Gift of the Spirit of Wisdom and Revelation</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 1:15"/>
    Because of this, ever since I learned about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all of God’s people,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 1:16"/>
    I have not stopped expressing gratitude for you, continually mentioning you in my prayers.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 1:17"/>
    I pray that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father who possesses all glory, would give you the Spirit who imparts wisdom and revelation, enabling you to know Him more fully.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 1:18"/>
    I pray that the eyes of your heart would be flooded with light, so that you would understand the hope to which He has called you, the glorious wealth of the inheritance He has reserved for His people,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 1:19"/>
    and the immeasurably great power available to us who believe, power that operates according to the working of His overwhelming might.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 1:20"/>
    This is the same mighty strength He exerted in Christ when He raised Him from death and placed Him at His right hand in the heavenly realm,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 1:21"/>
    positioning Him far above every authority and power and force and lordship, and above every title that can be given, not only in this present age but also in the age that is yet to come.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 1:22"/>
    God has placed all things in subjection under His feet and appointed Him as supreme head over everything for the benefit of the church,
    <verse eid="EPH 1:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EPH 1:23"/>
    which is His body, the fullness of Him who completely fills everything in every way.
    <verse eid="EPH 1:23"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="EPH 2"/>
  <para style="s1">Saved By Grace Through Faith</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 2:1"/>
    You were spiritually dead because of your transgressions and sins,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 2:2"/>
    the way of life in which you once conducted yourselves, following the pattern of this present world system, under the influence of the ruler who governs the spiritual realm of the air, the spirit who is now actively working in those who are characterised by disobedience to God.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 2:3"/>
    We all once conducted ourselves among them in the cravings of our fallen nature, carrying out the desires of the flesh and of the mind, and we were by our very nature children destined for God’s wrath, just like everyone else.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 2:4"/>
    But God, who has abundant mercy, because of the great love with which He loved us,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 2:5"/>
    even while we were dead in our transgressions, made us alive together with Christ—it is by grace that you have been saved—
    <verse eid="EPH 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 2:6"/>
    and He raised us up together with Him and seated us together with Him in the heavenly realm in Christ Jesus,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 2:7"/>
    in order that in the ages to come He might demonstrate the surpassing riches of His grace expressed in kindness towards us in Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 2:8"/>
    For it is by grace you have been saved through faith, and this salvation is not something that originates from yourselves; it is God’s gift to you,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 2:9"/>
    not something earned by works, so that no one has grounds for boasting.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 2:10"/>
    For we are His creative masterpiece, created in Christ Jesus to live out the good works that God prepared in advance for us to walk in.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Unity of the Jewish and Gentile Saints in Christ Jesus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 2:11"/>
    Therefore, remember that formerly you who are Gentiles by physical birth—referred to as “the uncircumcised” by those who call themselves “the circumcised” because of a physical operation performed by human hands—
    <verse eid="EPH 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 2:12"/>
    recall that at that time you existed apart from Christ, excluded from citizenship in Israel, and foreigners to the covenants that contained God’s promise, living without hope and without God in the world.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 2:13"/>
    But now in Christ Jesus, you who were once distant have been brought near through the blood of Christ.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 2:14"/>
    For He Himself is our peace, the One who made both groups into one and demolished the dividing wall, the hostility, through His physical death,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 2:15"/>
    by rendering powerless the Law with its commandments expressed in regulations, so that in Himself He might create one new humanity out of the two groups, thereby establishing peace,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 2:16"/>
    and might reconcile both groups to God in one body through the cross, having put to death the hostility through Himself.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 2:17"/>
    Then He came and proclaimed the good news of peace to you who were far away and peace to those who were near.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 2:18"/>
    For through Him we both have access by one Spirit to come into the Father’s presence.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 2:19"/>
    Consequently, you are no longer strangers and foreigners, but you are fellow citizens with God’s people and members of God’s household,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 2:20"/>
    built on the foundation laid by the apostles and prophets, with Christ Jesus Himself as the cornerstone,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 2:21"/>
    in whom the entire structure, being joined together, continues to grow into a holy sanctuary in the Lord,
    <verse eid="EPH 2:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 2:22"/>
    in whom you also are being constructed together into a dwelling place where God lives by the Spirit.
    <verse eid="EPH 2:22"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="EPH 3"/>
  <para style="s1">The Revelation of the Mystery of Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 3:1"/>
    For this reason, I, Paul, am a prisoner of Christ Jesus for the sake of you Gentiles—
    <verse eid="EPH 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 3:2"/>
    if indeed you have heard about the stewardship of God’s grace that was entrusted to me for your benefit,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 3:3"/>
    that the mystery was made known to me through direct revelation, just as I briefly wrote previously.
    <verse eid="EPH 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 3:4"/>
    By reading this, you will be able to perceive my understanding of the mystery concerning Christ,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 3:5"/>
    which was not made known to people in past generations as it has now been revealed to His holy apostles and prophets by the Spirit:
    <verse eid="EPH 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 3:6"/>
    specifically, that the Gentiles are fellow heirs and fellow members of the same body and fellow participants in the promise in Christ Jesus through the gospel,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 3:7"/>
    of which I became a servant according to the gift of God’s grace given to me through the operation of His power.
    <verse eid="EPH 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 3:8"/>
    To me, though I am the least significant of all God’s people, this grace was granted: to proclaim to the Gentiles the unfathomable riches found in Christ,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 3:9"/>
    and to make clear to everyone what is the plan of the mystery that was hidden throughout past ages in God who created all things,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 3:10"/>
    so that now through the church the multifaceted wisdom of God might be made known to the rulers and authorities in the heavenly realms,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 3:11"/>
    according to the eternal purpose that He carried out in Christ Jesus our Lord,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 3:12"/>
    in whom we possess bold confidence and the privilege of approaching God with assurance through faith in Him.
    <verse eid="EPH 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 3:13"/>
    Therefore I ask you not to become discouraged because of my sufferings on your behalf, which actually bring honour to you.
    <verse eid="EPH 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer for Attaining to All the Fullness of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 3:14"/>
    For this reason I kneel before the Father,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 3:15"/>
    from whom every family in heaven and on earth receives its identity,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 3:16"/>
    asking that He would grant you, according to the riches of His glory, to be strengthened with power through His Spirit in your inner being,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 3:17"/>
    so that Christ would make His home in your hearts through faith, and that you, being firmly rooted and established in love,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 3:18"/>
    would have the strength to grasp fully, along with all the saints, what is the breadth and length and height and depth of God’s love,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 3:19"/>
    and to experientially grasp the love of Christ—a love that transcends human understanding—so that you may be filled to all the fullness of God.
    <verse eid="EPH 3:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 3:20"/>
    Now to the One who has the power to accomplish infinitely beyond all things we request or conceive, working through His mighty power that operates within us,
    <verse eid="EPH 3:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 3:21"/>
    to Him belongs all glory in the church and in Christ Jesus through every generation, for all eternity. Amen.
    <verse eid="EPH 3:21"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="EPH 4"/>
  <para style="s1">Unity in the Body of Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 4:1"/>
    I therefore, as a prisoner because of my service to the Lord, urge you to conduct your lives in a way that reflects the high calling you have received,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 4:2"/>
    demonstrating complete humility and gentleness, with patient endurance, showing tolerance towards one another in love,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 4:3"/>
    making every effort to preserve the unity that the Spirit creates through the bond of peace.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 4:4"/>
    There is one body and one Spirit, just as you were called to one hope when God called you—
    <verse eid="EPH 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 4:5"/>
    one Lord, one faith, one baptism,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 4:6"/>
    one God and Father of all people, who rules over all and works through all and dwells in all.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 4:7"/>
    Yet to each individual among us grace has been given in proportion to the measure of Christ’s gift.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 4:8"/>
    This is why Scripture says,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“When He ascended to the heights,</para>
  <para style="p">He took captives in His train;</para>
  <para style="p">He distributed gifts to people.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 4:9"/>
    (Now this reference to His ascension implies that He also descended into the lower regions, the earth itself.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 4:10"/>
    He who descended is the very same One who ascended far above all the heavens, in order to fill the entire universe.)
    <verse eid="EPH 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 4:11"/>
    So He personally gave the apostles, and the prophets, and the evangelists, and the pastors and teachers,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 4:12"/>
    for the purpose of equipping God’s people for works of service, so that the body of Christ would be built up,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 4:13"/>
    until we all reach unity in the faith and in the knowledge of the Son of God, arriving at mature manhood, measured by nothing less than the full stature of Christ.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 4:14"/>
    Then we will no longer be immature children, shaken and tossed by the waves and swept along by every changing wind of teaching—by human cleverness and by craftiness deliberately designed to lead us progressively into error. 
    <verse eid="EPH 4:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 4:15"/>
    Instead, by speaking the truth in love, we are to grow up in every way into Him who is the head, namely Christ,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 4:16"/>
    from whom the entire body, joined and held together by every supporting ligament, grows and builds itself up in love as each part does its work according to its proper function.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Living the New Life in Christ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 4:17"/>
    So I declare this and solemnly affirm it in the Lord: You must no longer live as the Gentiles live, in the emptiness of their reasoning,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 4:18"/>
    having their understanding darkened, being separated from the life of God because of the ignorance within them, which stems from the hardness of their hearts.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 4:19"/>
    They have lost all moral sensitivity and have abandoned themselves to sensuality, engaging in every form of impurity with an insatiable desire for more.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 4:20"/>
    But you did not learn Christ in this way—
    <verse eid="EPH 4:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 4:21"/>
    surely you heard about Him and were taught in Him, in accordance with the truth that is found in Jesus:
    <verse eid="EPH 4:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 4:22"/>
    that you must put off your former way of life, the old self that is being corrupted by its deceitful lusts;
    <verse eid="EPH 4:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EPH 4:23"/>
    that you must be renewed in the attitude of your mind,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EPH 4:24"/>
    and put on the new self, which God has created in conformity to His own character—marked by righteousness and holiness that arise from the truth. 
    <verse eid="EPH 4:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EPH 4:25"/>
    Therefore, having laid aside falsehood, each one must speak truthfully with his neighbour, for we are all members of one another.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="EPH 4:26"/>
    If you become angry, do not let it lead you into sin; do not let the sun set while you are still angry,
    <verse eid="EPH 4:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="EPH 4:27"/>
    and do not give the devil an opportunity.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EPH 4:28"/>
    The person who has been stealing must steal no longer; rather, he must work hard, doing honest labour with his own hands, so that he will have something to share with anyone in need.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="EPH 4:29"/>
    Allow no corrupting words to come from your mouth, but speak only what is beneficial for edifying others as the situation requires, so that your words will impart grace to those who hear.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:29"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EPH 4:30"/>
    And do not cause grief to God’s Holy Spirit, who has marked you with His seal until the day when your redemption is complete.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:30"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="EPH 4:31"/>
    Remove from your lives all bitterness, fury and rage, all brawling and verbal abuse, together with every kind of malicious intent.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:31"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EPH 4:32"/>
    Rather, show kindness and tender hearts towards one another, extending forgiveness to each other in the same way God extended forgiveness to you through Christ.
    <verse eid="EPH 4:32"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">8 Quoted from Ps. 68:18</para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="EPH 5"/>
  <para style="s1">Imitating God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 5:1"/>
    Therefore, pattern your lives after God, as children who are deeply loved by Him,
    <verse eid="EPH 5:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 5:2"/>
    and conduct yourselves in love, following the example of Christ who loved us and offered Himself on our behalf as a sacrificial offering to God, producing a pleasing fragrance. 
    <verse eid="EPH 5:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 5:3"/>
    But sexual immorality and every form of moral impurity or greediness must not even be mentioned among you, as befits those who belong to God—
    <verse eid="EPH 5:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 5:4"/>
    likewise, vulgar speech, empty babbling, or crude humour, which are inappropriate, but let thanksgiving characterise your speech instead.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 5:5"/>
    For you know with certainty that no person who is sexually immoral, morally impure, or greedy—which amounts to idolatry—possesses any inheritance in the kingdom that belongs to Christ and God.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 5:6"/>
    Do not allow anyone to mislead you with hollow reasoning, for God’s wrath falls upon the disobedient because of these very things.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 5:7"/>
    Therefore, do not associate yourselves with such people as their partners.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Light in the Lord</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 5:8"/>
    For at one time you yourselves were darkness, but now you exist as light in the Lord. Conduct yourselves as those who belong to the light
    <verse eid="EPH 5:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 5:9"/>
    (for the light produces fruit that consists of complete goodness, righteousness and truth),
    <verse eid="EPH 5:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 5:10"/>
    carefully examining what brings pleasure to the Lord.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 5:11"/>
    Take no part in the barren works that belong to darkness, but instead bring them into the open.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 5:12"/>
    For even to speak of what they practise in hiding brings shame.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 5:13"/>
    But when anything is brought into the open by the light, it becomes visible and clear, for whatever makes things visible is light.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 5:14"/>
    Therefore it says,
    <verse eid="EPH 5:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Awaken, you who sleep,</para>
  <para style="p">and rise up from among the dead,</para>
  <para style="p">and Christ will give you light.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 5:15"/>
    Pay careful attention, therefore, to how you conduct your lives—not as those lacking wisdom but as those who possess it,
    <verse eid="EPH 5:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 5:16"/>
    seizing every opportunity wisely, for the times are characterised by evil.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 5:17"/>
    For this reason, do not lack in understanding, but grasp what the Lord desires.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Results of Being Filled with the Spirit</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 5:18"/>
    Do not become intoxicated with wine, for that path leads to debauchery; rather, keep being filled with the Spirit,
    <verse eid="EPH 5:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 5:19"/>
    speaking to each other through psalms and hymns and songs inspired by the Spirit, singing and making melodies in your hearts directed to the Lord,
    <verse eid="EPH 5:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 5:20"/>
    continually expressing gratitude to God the Father for everything, doing so in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ,
    <verse eid="EPH 5:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 5:21"/>
    yielding to one another in reverent fear of Christ:
    <verse eid="EPH 5:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 5:22"/>
    Wives, yield to your own husbands as an expression of your submission to the Lord,
    <verse eid="EPH 5:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EPH 5:23"/>
    because the husband functions as head over the wife in the same way that Christ functions as head over the church, being Himself the deliverer of the body.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EPH 5:24"/>
    Now just as the church places itself under Christ’s authority, so wives should place themselves under their husbands’ authority in all matters.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EPH 5:25"/>
    Husbands, demonstrate love towards your wives in the same manner that Christ demonstrated love towards the church and surrendered Himself on her behalf
    <verse eid="EPH 5:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="EPH 5:26"/>
    in order to consecrate her, having purified her through the cleansing that comes by water accompanied by the spoken word,
    <verse eid="EPH 5:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="EPH 5:27"/>
    so that He might present the church to Himself in splendour, having neither blemish nor wrinkle nor anything of that kind, but rather that she would be consecrated and without defect.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="EPH 5:28"/>
    Husbands ought to demonstrate love towards their own wives in this same manner, treating them as their own bodies. The man who demonstrates love towards his wife demonstrates love towards himself.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="EPH 5:29"/>
    For no person has ever despised his own flesh, but rather provides nourishment for it and cares for it tenderly, just as Christ does for the church—
    <verse eid="EPH 5:29"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="EPH 5:30"/>
    because we are parts of His body.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:30"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="EPH 5:31"/>
    “For this cause a man shall depart from his father and mother and be joined to his wife, and the two shall become one flesh.”*
    <verse eid="EPH 5:31"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="EPH 5:32"/>
    This mystery holds great significance—I am applying it to Christ and the church.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:32"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="EPH 5:33"/>
    In any case, each individual husband among you must love his own wife as he loves himself, and the wife must show reverence for her husband.
    <verse eid="EPH 5:33"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">14 The source of this quote is unknown, but there are allusions to several Old Testament texts of Is. 26:19; 51:17; 52:1; 60:1; Mal. 4:2</para>
  <para style="p">31 Quoted from Gen. 2:24</para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="EPH 6"/>
  <para style="s1">Children and Parents</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 6:1"/>
    Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this represents right conduct.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 6:2"/>
    “Give honour to your father and mother”—this is the first commandment that carries a promise with it—
    <verse eid="EPH 6:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 6:3"/>
    “in order that things may go well for you and that you may live many years on the earth.”
    <verse eid="EPH 6:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 6:4"/>
    And fathers, do not exasperate your children, but raise them with the discipline and guidance that come from the Lord.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Slaves and Masters</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 6:5"/>
    Slaves, render obedience to those who are your masters in the physical realm, approaching them with fear and trembling and with genuine sincerity of heart, as though serving Christ Himself,
    <verse eid="EPH 6:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 6:6"/>
    not merely when they are watching you and in order to gain their approval, but as those who serve Christ, accomplishing God’s will from the depths of your being.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 6:7"/>
    Carry out your service with eager willingness, as though rendering it to the Lord rather than to human beings,
    <verse eid="EPH 6:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 6:8"/>
    understanding that each person will receive back from the Lord whatever good deed he performs, whether he is a slave or a free person.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 6:9"/>
    And masters, demonstrate the same attitude towards them, ceasing from threats, recognising that the One who is Master over both them and you resides in heaven, and with Him there exists no partiality.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Complete Armour of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 6:10"/>
    Finally, draw your strength from the Lord and from the power of His overwhelming might.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 6:11"/>
    Clothe yourselves with the complete equipment that God provides, enabling you to hold your position against the deceptive strategies of the devil.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 6:12"/>
    For the battle we fight is not directed against human opponents, but against the rulers, against the authorities, against the world powers governing this present darkness, against the spiritual forces that promote evil in the heavenly realm.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 6:13"/>
    Because of this, take up the complete equipment that God provides, so that you will have the ability to resist when the evil day arrives, and having accomplished everything necessary, to remain standing.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 6:14"/>
    Take your stand, then, having fastened the belt of truth around your waist, having clothed yourself with the breastplate that righteousness provides,
    <verse eid="EPH 6:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 6:15"/>
    having strapped on your feet the readiness that the gospel of peace supplies.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 6:16"/>
    Beyond all these things, take hold of the shield that faith provides, by means of which you will have the power to extinguish every flaming arrow that the evil one launches.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 6:17"/>
    Accept the helmet that salvation provides and the sword that the Spirit supplies, which is God’s spoken word.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 6:18"/>
    Through every kind of prayer and petition, pray at all times in the Spirit, and towards this end remain vigilant with complete persistence and petition on behalf of all who are God’s people.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 6:19"/>
    Pray also on my behalf, that the right message would be given to me whenever I open my mouth, enabling me to proclaim fearlessly the hidden truth of the gospel,
    <verse eid="EPH 6:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 6:20"/>
    for which I serve as an ambassador, though I am bound with chains. Pray that in proclaiming it I would speak with the boldness that my duty requires.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Final Greetings and Benediction</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 6:21"/>
    Now in order that you may also have knowledge of my circumstances and what I am doing, Tychicus, my beloved brother and dependable servant in the Lord, will provide you with all the information.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 6:22"/>
    I have sent him to you for this precise purpose, that you might learn about our situation and that he might bring encouragement to your hearts.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EPH 6:23"/>
    Peace to the brothers and sisters, along with love combined with faith, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="EPH 6:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EPH 6:24"/>
    May grace be present with all who love our Lord Jesus Christ with an uncorrupted and enduring love. 
    <verse eid="EPH 6:24"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 6"/>
</usx>
